00:36:39.420 --> 00:37:10.530
<v Ira Glass>We've arrived at act four of our show. Act Four, Paradise Lost. There are certain settings-- as we've said on the show already-- where making judgments about people from tiny amounts of evidence is kind of required-- if you're interviewing somebody for a job, if you are choosing who is going to adopt your baby. Being on vacation is not one of those situations. But some people really never can stop the judging, like, apparently, one of our regular contributors, Shalom Auslander.
<v Ira Glass>我们已经到了节目的第四幕。第四幕，失落的天堂。正如我们在节目中已经说过的，某些环境下——如果你正在面试某人，如果你正在选择谁要领养你的孩子——根据极少量证据对人做出判断是某种必需的。度假不是那种情况。但有些人真的永远无法停止评判，就像我们的一位常客，沙洛姆·奥斯兰德，显然也是这样。

00:37:10.530 --> 00:37:51.140
<v Shalom Auslander>I ruin vacations. That's just what I do. In Greece, I was sure the hotel had stuck us with the worst room in the building, even though every room was identical. I know that because we switched three times the day we got there. We switched again the morning after, and went home two days early. A year later, I spent four days in a Jamaican rain forest complaining about the weather. We're in a rain forest, my wife said. So? So it rains. We went home two days early.
<v Shalom Auslander>我毁掉了假期。这就是我做的。在希腊，我确信酒店给了我们楼里最差的房间，尽管每个房间都一模一样。我知道那是因为我们到的那天换了三次。第二天早上我们又换了，并提前两天回家了。一年后，我在牙买加雨林待了四天，抱怨天气。我们在雨林里，我妻子说。那又怎样？所以它会下雨。我们提前两天回家了。

00:37:51.140 --> 00:38:13.650
<v Shalom Auslander>And so last year, when my wife informed me that she had booked us a six-day vacation in Anguilla, a remote island in the British West Indies, I decided that this time would be different. It was our first trip in a while, and I'd been doing a lot of work on myself. With the money I'd spent on therapy, I could have bought the whole damn island of Anguilla. So I was anxious to see how far I'd come.
<v Shalom Auslander>所以去年，当我妻子通知我她为我们预订了在安圭拉岛的六天假期，那是英属西印度群岛中一个偏远的岛屿时，我决定这次会不同。这是我们一段时间以来的第一次旅行，我一直在进行自我建设。我花在心理治疗上的钱，本来可以买下整个该死的安圭拉岛。所以我很想看看我进步了多少。

00:38:13.650 --> 00:38:41.200
<v Shalom Auslander>The resort was far more expensive than we could afford. I suspected that my wife was hoping that an exclusive resort would minimize the number of disappointments that could inevitably set me off. There was no need for her to worry. This time would be different. This time, I would be different.
