00:41:04.240 --> 00:41:47.160
<v Shalom Auslander>Could have been 1982, Marvin continued, or maybe even 1978, now that I think about it. No, no, it was 1980. I remember because I was arguing with my wife about Reagan. Whoo boy, did she hate him. Uh-huh, I said. I looked toward the beach and could see my wife and son running down to the water with his pail and shovel. Well, I better go. Family's waiting for me and all. She's dead now, he said. He gently cleared his throat and looked to the ground. Damn it, I thought. I'm sorry, I said. She was a good woman, he said. I nodded. I'm sure, I said.
<v Shalom Auslander>“可能是1982年，”马文继续说，“或者甚至1978年，现在我想起来了。不，不，是1980年。我记得因为我当时在和妻子吵关于里根的事。天哪，她多讨厌他。”“嗯哼，”我说。我望向海滩，可以看到我的妻子和儿子拿着小桶和铲子朝水边跑去。“好吧，我得走了。家人在等我什么的。”“她现在去世了，”他说。他轻轻清了清嗓子，看向地面。“该死，”我心想。“我很遗憾，”我说。“她是个好女人，”他说。我点点头。“我相信，”我说。“

00:41:47.160 --> 00:42:25.730
<v Shalom Auslander>The hotel was very different back then, of course, Marvin continued. Very, very different. The restaurant wasn't where it is now. No, sir. That building wasn't even built until 1990, or so. Maybe '92, even. A fellow named Jeremiah built it with his own two hands, by gosh. Nobody builds like that anymore. As Marvin rambled on, I began to wonder, was there any way I could switch rooms without upsetting my wife? But I stopped myself, pulled myself together. Not this time, I thought. We are having a pleasant vacation.
<v Shalom Auslander>“那时候酒店很不一样，当然，”马文继续说。“非常，非常不一样。餐厅不在现在这个地方。不，先生。那栋楼直到1990年左右才建成。甚至可能是92年。一个叫杰里米的人用他自己的双手建成的，天哪。现在没人那样盖房子了。”当马文喋喋不休时，我开始怀疑，有没有什么办法能在不惹恼我妻子的前提下换房间？但我阻止了自己，调整了心态。不是这次，我想。我们要度过一个愉快的假期。

00:42:25.730 --> 00:43:11.470
<v Shalom Auslander>Is that your wife, Marvin asked. Yeah, I said, waiting for me. She's beautiful, said Marvin. Yeah, I said. Well, I better skedaddle. My wife was beautiful too. Uh-huh, I said with a wave. Well, I'll see you later. Marvin waved back, walked up the steps of the villa directly adjoining ours, took out his key and walked inside. The door closed and the expectorating began. [COUGHING] Damn it, I thought.
